---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Rules" description="Glitched Network server rules.">
    <main class="legal-page">
        <article>
            <h1 class="font-PressStart2P">Rules</h1>
            <p>These rules keep Glitched SMP fair, playable, and welcoming. Staff may act on behavior that harms the server even when it is not listed word-for-word here.</p>

            <h2>Respect Players</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>No harassment, hate speech, threats, or targeted drama.</li>
                <li>Keep chat usable. Do not spam, advertise, impersonate staff, or intentionally stir conflict.</li>
                <li>Do not share another player's private information.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Play Fair</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>No hacked clients, x-ray, macros, dupes, exploits, or automation that gives an unfair advantage.</li>
                <li>Report bugs or economy issues instead of abusing them.</li>
                <li>Alternate accounts may be restricted if used to evade punishments or bypass progression limits.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Protect Builds</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>No griefing, stealing, trapping, or destroying another player's work without permission.</li>
                <li>Respect claims, bases, farms, shops, public builds, and event areas.</li>
                <li>Lag machines and intentionally harmful redstone are not allowed.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Staff Decisions</h2>
            <p>Staff may warn, mute, kick, ban, roll back damage, or remove items when needed. If you believe a punishment was wrong, make an appeal through the community Discord and include clear context.</p>
        </article>
    </main>
</MainLayout>
